  "cause_conclusions": {
    "direct_reproduction": "Original full metadata command, executed by the producer in an isolated core cwd, changed the fixed root lock to exactly the bytes retained from the failed real build.",
    "not_claimed": "The original failed build was not process/file-write traced; attribution combines its exact changed bytes with the isolated command reproduction and compile-time macro call chain.",
    "retracted_candidate": "OSDK util --no-deps metadata was only a preliminary static suspicion. Six real producer counterexamples left the root seed unchanged and do not support that path as the writer.",
    "call_chain": "aster-core init calls parse_metadata!; parse_metadata calls component_generate and get_component_toml_path, and both call full metadata. init_component itself does not call metadata.",
    "correct_fix_scope": "Retain complete component package enumeration. Keep the original Git lock blob and SHA as the seed; explicitly verify the unique local working-lock derivative; use full metadata --locked.",
    "assumption_correction": "The initial implementation assumption that the working root Cargo.lock could remain byte-identical to upstream while adding this dependency was contradicted by real full metadata resolution.",
    "implementation_status": "Approved fix and post-fix execution are reviewed separately; this saved-evidence receipt is not a passing kernel test or fixed-build acceptance."
  },
